From f0bf1527b9d305eedf04ed0aa24c4f03fcf60cc8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 17:29:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] XP lock: any skill, from the stats tab, and it never waives a
 requirement

Right-click any skill box for "Toggle <Skill> XP-lock" beside its guide option,
confirm, and that skill stops gaining experience. Its hover panel says "XP locked"
in red where it said "Next Level At:".

The lock is one perm varp, a bitmask at each skill's own stat id, and the engine
reads it in Player.addXp - the same place the XP rate went, and for the same reason:
290 stat_advance call sites, no wrapper proc, so anything content-side would have to
be added to every one and missed by the next skill written. A quest's lump sum is
refused exactly like a log: the items still arrive and the quest still completes.

What it deliberately does not do is waive anything. A lock never touches a level, so
every requirement that reads stat(...) reads the same number - a pure with Attack
locked is still refused the dragon mace. Battery group 11 holds that line by proving
nothing outside scripts/gamemodes/ can even see %xp_locked.

The new buttons are emitted BEFORE the guide buttons on purpose. The left-click
action is the LAST option appended, so a lock button after the guide would put
locking one stray click away.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
